### ============================================================
### PART 2: Full integration test via main-backend (port 8080)
### main-backend fetches from DB → sends to side-backend → returns results
### ============================================================

### [8] Login first — token is auto-saved to @token variable
POST {{mainBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nationalId": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

###

### [9] 🔗 FULL INTEGRATION — trigger scheduling via main-backend
### main-backend (8080) reads DB, calls side-backend (8081), saves results
### Replace {{token}} with the accessToken from step [8]
POST {{mainBaseUrl}}/api/schedule/run?strategy=GREEDY
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [10] ROUND_ROBIN via main-backend
POST {{mainBaseUrl}}/api/schedule/run?strategy=ROUND_ROBIN
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [11] 📏 CONSTRAINT_PROGRAMMING via side-backend (Direct Test)
### Should return 200 OK with valid schedule or empty strict result
POST {{sideBaseUrl}}/api/v1/algo/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "strategy": "CONSTRAINT_PROGRAMMING",
  "users": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "firstName": "Alice",
      "lastName": "Smith",
      "email": "alice@example.com",
      "dailyAvailabilityHours": 8,
      "maxTasks": 5,
      "roles": ["WORKER"],
      "vacations": []
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Strict Task",
      "durationHours": 4,
